While speaking with Insider, screenwriter&nbsp;
Akela Cooper praised Johnstone for adding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:11.760
value to M3GAN's terrifying nature by&nbsp;
adding the dance sequence. Cooper said:

00:02:21.468 --> 00:02:27.000
Allison Williams, who both stars in and executive&nbsp;
produced the film, told Entertainment Weekly that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.000 --> 00:02:31.680
the team had their own strategy to make the dance&nbsp;
scene a viral sensation. Williams told the outlet:

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:49.920
Marketing M3GAN with the dance sequence clearly&nbsp;
paid dividends as the film went on to make a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.920 --> 00:02:55.500
whopping $30 million domestically during its&nbsp;
opening weekend. How much of M3GAN's box office&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.500 --> 00:03:00.360
glory can be attributed to the viral nature of&nbsp;
the dance sequence? It's hard to quantify but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:04.800
take to social media and viewers will find&nbsp;
thousands of memes and fancams of M3GAN,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.360
with the dance sequence dominating the&nbsp;
conversation. It's hard imagining the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:13.200
buzz surrounding the film being so loud if&nbsp;
the dance sequence wasn't in the trailer.

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:17.460
While speaking with The Hollywood Reporter,&nbsp;
Allison Williams admitted that the film's&nbsp;&nbsp;

